cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Convergence of the random Abelian sandpile: Lean formalization"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Random-Abelian-Sandpile"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Convergence of the random Abelian sandpile" by
  Ahmed Bou-Rabee, in a corrected draft of the arXiv source kept in paper/. All 28 numbered results
  are proved in Lean, with no sorry and only the standard axioms: 19 outright and 9 from six results
  of the literature that enter as explicit hypotheses. Among them are the main theorem (sandpiles
  started from a random high-density background in nW converge, after rescaling, to the solution of
  an obstacle problem for a deterministic degenerate elliptic operator), its analogue with the open
  boundary condition, and a corrected form of the single-source theorem with a recurrent effective
  operator. Theorems 1.1 and 9.2 have Mathlib-only comparator challenges.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - abelian sandpile
  - stochastic homogenization
  - viscosity solutions
